<title>GERMANY: Daimler-no acute need for capital hike in next yrs.</title>
<headline>Daimler-no acute need for capital hike in next yrs.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daimler-Benz AG chief financial officer Manfred Gentz said on Wednesday he saw no need for the industrial group to increase its capital in coming years.</p>
<p>&quot;We see no acute reason for a traditional capital increase in the coming years,&quot; Gentz told the company's annual news conference.</p>
<p>Daimler said earlier that it planned to issue 1.1 billion marks in 5.75 percent mandatory convertible notes due June 14, 2002.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
